{x_bookshelf
    {message
        output={@

The bookshelf is set into the east wall so its sides and back are made of
the same paneling as the room. The shelves are thick glass panes with small
spotlights shining down on them.

There are some abstract sculptures on a couple of the shelves.
A handful of books on another, held upright by two brass deer heads with
exaggeratedly large antlers.

        }
    }
}

{x_on_bookshelf
    {message
        output={@

There are some abstract sculptures on a couple of the shelves.
A handful of books on another, held upright by two brass deer heads with
exaggeratedly large antlers.

        }
    }
}



{x_books
    {message
        output={@

You examine the few books that are on the shelf.
There are a couple of business and philosophy books.
An old sailor's journal and a book on cybersecurity.

        }
    }
}

{x_on_books
    {message
        output={@

There is nothing on the books.

        }
    }
}

{x_under_books
    {message
        output={@

You go through, lifting each book.
You don't see anything.

        }
    }
}

{x_behind_books
    {message
        output={@

There isn't anything behind the books.

        }
    }
}


{x_cybersec_book
    {message
        output={@

You thumb through the cybersecurity book.
One of the pages has been dog eared. You turn there and read.
It is an article describing attacking the MT19937 pseudo random generator using
a system of equations with bit vectors.

        }
    }
}

// https://www.schutzwerk.com/blog/attacking-a-rng/






{input, syntax=[tplt_syntax]((x_your_bookshelf))
    {act, logic=x_bookshelf, tags=!_type|room }
}

{input, syntax=[tplt_syntax]((x_on_your_bookshelf))
    {act, logic=x_on_bookshelf, tags=!_type|room }
}


{input, syntax=[tplt_syntax]((x_books))
    {act, logic=x_books, tags=!_type|room }
}

{input, syntax=[tplt_syntax]((x_on_books))
    {act, logic=x_on_books, tags=!_type|room }
}

{input, syntax=[tplt_syntax]((x_under_books))
    {act, logic=x_under_books, tags=!_type|room }
}

{input, syntax=[tplt_syntax]((x_behind_books))
    {act, logic=x_behind_books, tags=!_type|room }
}


{input, syntax=[tplt_syntax]((x_cybersec_book))
    {act, logic=x_cybersec_book, tags=!_type|room }
}
